# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit the real file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000
LOG_LEVEL=info

# AES-256-GCM key for encrypting persisted carrier sessions at rest.
# Generate with:  openssl rand -hex 32
SESSION_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Residential egress
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL. Leave empty and everything still runs — the demo portal needs no proxy,
# and a real GEICO login has been verified working without one from a home connection.
# It becomes effectively required once HOSTED: datacenter IP ranges (AWS/GCP/Fly/Render)
# are published and pre-flagged, so carriers block them.
#
# Pay-as-you-go options with instant signup: Decodo (~$4/GB), IPRoyal, Proxy-Cheap.
#
#   RESIDENTIAL_PROXY_URL=http://USER:PASS@HOST:PORT
#
# Take the host, port and credentials from your provider's dashboard. Note that HOST is
# a per-proxy address on a dedicated-IP plan, not a shared gateway hostname — those are
# two different products, and which one you have changes the next setting.
#
# For Proxy-Cheap you do not have to transcribe them. Set PROXYCHEAP_API_KEY and
# PROXYCHEAP_API_SECRET below and run:
#
#     npm run proxy:discover
#
# which reads the account and prints the exact line to paste here, with the port
# already matched to the proxy's `proxyType`. That matters: one proxy object can carry
# httpPort, httpsPort and socks5Port at once, they are not interchangeable, and picking
# the wrong one fails at connect time in a way that looks like a blocked IP.
RESIDENTIAL_PROXY_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which kind of proxy product the URL above points at: dedicated | rotating
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This decides whether PROXY_USERNAME_TEMPLATE below should be set AT ALL, and the two
# answers are opposite. Leave it unset only if you genuinely do not know.
#
#   dedicated   One fixed exit IP (Proxy-Cheap RESIDENTIAL_STATIC / ISP, dedicated
#               datacenter, pinned mobile). Stickiness is a property of what you bought.
#               PROXY_USERNAME_TEMPLATE MUST STAY EMPTY — there is no session concept,
#               and a template rewrites a username the provider expects verbatim.
#
#   rotating    A gateway hostname fronting a pool. The only way to hold one IP for a
#               whole pull is a provider-specific sticky-session username, so
#               PROXY_USERNAME_TEMPLATE IS REQUIRED.
#
# `npm run proxy:discover` determines this from the account and prints the right value.
PROXY_MODEL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Proxy-Cheap management API (OPTIONAL — tooling only, never needed to serve)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Auth is two headers: X-Api-Key and X-Api-Secret. Get them from the dashboard.
# Used by `npm run proxy:discover` and `npm run proxy:autoextend` to read the account,
# derive the settings above, and check expiry before a run rather than during one.
#
# DO NOT SET THESE IN PRODUCTION. This key pair can order proxies, extend periods and
# buy bandwidth — it spends money. The serving process never reads it, and `npm run
# doctor` treats its absence as fine. What the browser authenticates to the proxy with
# is inside RESIDENTIAL_PROXY_URL; keeping the two apart means a compromised deployment
# leaks proxy access, not billing access.
PROXYCHEAP_API_KEY=
PROXYCHEAP_API_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sticky sessions — get this wrong and it fails SILENTLY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# {session} is replaced with a per-pull token so login -> MFA -> document fetch all
# leave from one IP. A pull spans 30s to several minutes because a human is reading a
# text message, and if the IP changes in that window the carrier sees a session hop
# between cities and invalidates it.
#
# The important part: a WRONG template does not error. Residential gateways parse the
# username, apply the flags they recognise, and ignore the rest — so a typo gives you
# a working proxy that rotates on every connection. The failure then surfaces three
# layers away as "your session expired" or a repeated MFA challenge, pointing at
# cookies or anti-bot rather than at a username.
#
# So VERIFY IT rather than trusting it:
#
#     npm run proxy:verify
#
# That holds one session for 45s, confirms the IP never changes, and separately
# confirms a *different* session gets a *different* IP — which is what distinguishes
# working stickiness from an account that simply has one static exit.
#
# Formats differ per provider and there is no standard. Known shapes:
#   Decodo       USER-session-{session}-sessionduration-10
#   IPRoyal      USER_session-{session}_lifetime-10m
#   Bright Data  USER-session-{session}
#   Shifter      USER-sid-{session}-ttl-600
#
# Proxy-Cheap is NOT in that list on purpose. Their residential-static product is a
# dedicated exit IP, so it needs no template and setting one breaks authentication.
# An earlier version of this file suggested `{user}-session-{session}` for Proxy-Cheap;
# that was a guess, it was wrong for this product, and `GET /proxies` disproved it —
# the response has no session concept anywhere. If your Proxy-Cheap plan is a rotating
# gateway rather than a static IP, get the syntax from the dashboard and verify it.
#
# LEAVE THIS EMPTY when PROXY_MODEL=dedicated. Do not spend a real carrier login on an
# unverified template — a failed attempt counts against account lockout limits.
#
# `{user}` interpolates the username from RESIDENTIAL_PROXY_URL, so credentials stay
# in one place.
#
# Choose a session lifetime longer than your worst-case pull. MFA_WAIT_TIMEOUT_MS
# allows 180s for a human, so a 10-minute lifetime is a sensible floor; a 1-minute
# one will drop mid-flow.
PROXY_USERNAME_TEMPLATE=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Browser
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# patchright = stealth-patched Playwright (default). playwright = fallback.
BROWSER_DRIVER=patchright

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HEADLESS=false is REQUIRED for GEICO. This is a measured finding, not taste.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GEICO's POST /ws/login/authenticate returns:
#
#     302  under headless   -> the SPA cannot follow it, login silently stalls
#     200  headed           -> login proceeds normally
#
# Same machine, same IP, same browser binary, no proxy either way. Headless was
# the only variable. In 677 captured responses from a working session, the only
# 3xx were ad pixels -- a GEICO /ws/ endpoint never redirects. See F-40.
#
# "Headed" does NOT mean a window on a server. In Docker the entrypoint runs the
# app under Xvfb, a virtual display: full real Chrome, no window anywhere. You
# only see windows when running locally on a machine with a real display.
#
# Setting this to true makes deployment marginally simpler and breaks GEICO.
# Progressive and the demo portal work either way.
HEADLESS=false

# One browser per host. Headed Chrome costs ~80-150MB more RSS than headless, so
# raising this needs a matching memory increase wherever you run it — a larger EC2
# instance type, or a higher container memory limit. An OOM kill takes the whole
# process and every in-flight session with it, not just one tab.
BROWSER_POOL_SIZE=1
BLOCK_RESOURCES=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Timeouts (ms)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NAV_TIMEOUT_MS=20000
LOGIN_TIMEOUT_MS=45000
MFA_WAIT_TIMEOUT_MS=180000
DOCUMENT_TIMEOUT_MS=45000
SESSION_TTL_MS=900000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATA_DIR=./data
STORAGE_STATE_TTL_MS=43200000

# Self-hosted practice portal. Lets the whole flow be demoed with no credentials.
ENABLE_MOCK_CARRIER=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logging & diagnostics
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs are written by the app itself, not by shell redirection, so they exist
# regardless of how the process was started.
LOG_DIR=./logs
LOG_TO_FILE=true
LOG_MAX_BYTES=20971520
LOG_MAX_FILES=10
LOG_REQUESTS=true
LOG_FAILURE_BUNDLES=true

# Bearer token for /api/diagnostics/*. Minimum 16 chars.
# UNSET => those endpoints are loopback-only (fails closed, safe default).
# Required to pull logs off a deployed instance:
#   openssl rand -hex 24
DIAGNOSTICS_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which document to fetch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Maps onto the carrier's own document-category taxonomy — the same keys behind
# the portal's "Filter view:" dropdown (All | Billing | DecPage | Contract | ...).
#   contract     -> Policy Contracts   (category "Contract")
#   declarations -> Declarations Page  (category "DecPage")
#   idcard       -> Insurance ID cards (category "IdCard")
DOCUMENT_TARGET=contract

# How many to return. 1 means the single best match; returning several
# identically-titled PDFs and letting the user guess is not an answer.
DOCUMENT_LIMIT=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pre-warming
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keeps one anonymous page per carrier parked on the login form, so a COLD pull
# skips the context launch, navigation and SPA form render. Purely opportunistic:
# adoption falls back to a normal acquire on any doubt, and a stale page is
# discarded rather than typed into.
PREWARM_ENABLED=true
# How long a parked page stays adoptable. Bounded because carriers mint per-load
# tokens (Progressive issues a PingFederate flowId per login-page load).
PREWARM_TTL_MS=120000
